#: ../doc/titles.rst:23
msgid "Text & Titles"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/titles.rst:25
msgid "Adding text overlays, lower thirds, and titles is an important aspect of video editing, and OpenShot comes with an easy-to-use Title Editor. Use the Title menu (located in the main menu of OpenShot) to launch the Title Editor. You can also use the keyboard shortcut :kbd:`Ctrl+T`."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/titles.rst:29
msgid "Titles are simply vector image files with transparent backgrounds (``*.svg``). OpenShot comes with many easy-to-use templates, but you can also create your own or import new templates into OpenShot. These templates allow you to quickly change the text, font, size, color, and background color. You can also launch an advanced, external SVG editor for further customizations (if needed). Once the title is added to your project, drag and drop the title on a Track above a video clip. The transparent background will allow the video below to appear behind the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/titles.rst:38
msgid "Edit text directly in the preview"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/titles.rst:40
msgid "The quickest way to add text is to type it straight onto the video preview."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/titles.rst:42
msgid "Click **Tt** in the **Timeline** toolbar, choose **Title → Text**, or press :kbd:`Shift+T`. A text clip is added at the playhead, above the clips already there, and its placeholder text is selected, ready to replace by typing."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/titles.rst:45
msgid "Type your text. Press :kbd:`Shift+Enter` for a new line."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/titles.rst:46
msgid "Press :kbd:`Enter`, or click outside the text, to finish. Clicking anywhere else (the preview, the timeline, another dock), moving the playhead, or pressing Play also finishes and keeps your changes; the style bar and the **Properties** dock change the text without finishing. The clip then shows the normal transform handles to move, scale and rotate it. Press :kbd:`Escape` instead to remove a text you just added (or, when editing an existing text, to throw away this editing session)."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/titles.rst:53
msgid "To edit an existing text, double-click it in the preview, select its clip and press :kbd:`Enter`, or right-click the clip and choose **Text → Edit Text**. All of its text is selected, so typing replaces it. Starting playback or seeking ends editing without keeping unfinished changes, so press :kbd:`Enter` first to keep them."
msgstr ""

